│ patch_description        │ Replace the random cloud with a symmetric 14-point construction consisting of the 8       │
│                          │ vertices of a cube and 6 axis vertices.  The axis radius is chosen so that the largest    │
│                          │ axis-to-axis distance equals the largest axis-to-opposite-cube distance:                  │
│                          │ \(2a = \sqrt{(a+1)^2+2}\), giving \(a=(1+\sqrt{10})/3\).                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances the diameter constraints while retaining a comparatively large minimum      │
│                          │ distance.  The construction is deterministic, requires no optimization at evaluation      │
│                          │ time, has exactly 14 finite 3D points, and is substantially better conditioned than       │
│                          │ independent Gaussian samples.                                                             │
