│ patch_name               │ deterministic_maximin_relaxation                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the unstructured Gaussian sample with a deterministic multi-start maximin         │
│                          │ optimization specialized for the evaluator’s squared distance ratio.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new construction keeps the configuration centered and normalized after every update,  │
│                          │ which is valid because the objective is invariant under translation and uniform scaling.  │
│                          │ It then performs smooth extremal-distance ascent: close pairs receive repulsive forces    │
│                          │ while the currently largest pairs receive attractive forces.  The smoothing temperature   │
│                          │ is annealed, so early iterations improve the global distribution and late iterations      │
│                          │ increasingly target the actual minimum and maximum pairwise distances.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Several reproducible initial configurations are optimized, and the best configuration is  │
│                          │ selected using the evaluator’s exact squared ratio rather than the smoothed surrogate.    │
│                          │ This directly targets `(dmin / dmax)^2`, returns exactly fourteen finite 3D points, and   │
│                          │ avoids external optimization dependencies.                                                │
