│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ break_antipodal_symmetry                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The seven-line construction is close to the best possible *antipodal* packing, but its    │
│                          │ enforced antipodal symmetry prevents it from reaching configurations in which the 14      │
│                          │ points can move independently. The reference ratio is above the apparent                  │
│                          │ antipodal-line-packing plateau, so the final candidate should be refined as a general     │
│                          │ diameter-normalized 14-point packing.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit preserves the strong antipodal solution as a guaranteed incumbent, then applies │
│                          │ deterministic symmetry-breaking perturbations and direct optimization of all 91 squared   │
│                          │ pairwise distances. The optimization maximizes a smooth approximation of the log          │
│                          │ minimum-distance / maximum-distance objective. Centering and RMS normalization remove the │
│                          │ translation and scale null directions after each step. Candidates are always selected     │
│                          │ using the evaluator’s actual unsmoothed squared-distance ratio, so smoothing cannot cause │
│                          │ a worse result than the original antipodal construction.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0395                                                                                   │
