│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ analytic_twisted_prism                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This uses an analytic symmetry-reduced construction instead of iterative random           │
│                          │ optimization. The 14 points are arranged as two staggered regular hexagons and two poles. │
│                          │ The hexagons are rotated by 30 degrees, which distributes inter-layer contacts            │
│                          │ efficiently. Their radius and layer height are solved from contact equations so that the  │
│                          │ shortest same-ring and nearest cross-ring distances are equal, while the farthest         │
│                          │ cross-ring pairs equal the pole-to-pole diameter. This produces a highly balanced         │
│                          │ deterministic packing with no optimization-time overhead.                                 │
