│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ force_biased_local_search                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Augment the existing random one-point perturbations with contact-force-biased proposals.  │
│                          │ Near an optimal diameter packing, improvements are governed primarily by the shortest     │
│                          │ pairwise contacts.  For half of each batch, move the selected point away from nearby      │
│                          │ points using an inverse-fourth-power repulsive force, while retaining a small random      │
│                          │ component to break symmetric force cancellations.  The remaining proposals retain the     │
│                          │ original unbiased random moves, preserving exploration and avoiding reliance on the force │
│                          │ heuristic alone.  All candidates continue through the existing centering and diameter     │
│                          │ normalization, so the optimization remains exactly aligned with the evaluator objective.  │
