│ patch_description        │ Use a small continuation portfolio rather than applying one sharpness schedule to every   │
│                          │ initializer.  The diameter-packing objective is nonsmooth and different basins can        │
│                          │ benefit from different rates of concentration onto active contacts.  This edit preserves  │
│                          │ the successful quadratic 6-to-100 path, adds a slower 6-to-200 schedule, and adds a       │
│                          │ piecewise schedule that explores with moderate sharpness before focusing strongly on the  │
│                          │ final contact graph.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement also records the best exact ratio encountered during its trajectory.  At   │
│                          │ high sharpness, a smooth surrogate may occasionally make a final step that improves its   │
│                          │ surrogate but slightly worsens the true bottleneck ratio; returning the exact incumbent   │
│                          │ prevents that loss.  All schedules and seeds remain deterministic.                        │
