│                          │ schedules distributed across the existing multistarts. Distance-ratio packing objectives  │
│                          │ have many contact-graph basins, and the sharpness schedule materially affects which basin │
│                          │ is reached. The first schedule retains a gentle 6-to-100 quadratic path, the second       │
│                          │ delays concentration until a slower 6-to-200 path, and the third holds a moderate         │
│                          │ soft-extrema objective before rapidly focusing on active contacts. The existing           │
│                          │ exact-ratio selection and final high-sharpness polish compare all candidates without      │
│                          │ changing the returned format or adding random nondeterminism.                             │
