│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 16 Gaussian starts, 1500 iterations per start, a                │
│                          │ squared-distance soft-extrema temperature schedule from 0.09 to 0.025, and normalized     │
│                          │ gradient steps from 0.045 downward. Its main limitation is that most random starts do not │
│                          │ begin near strong diameter-packing contact graphs.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new configuration uses a structured portfolio centered on staggered                   │
│                          │ two-ring-plus-pole layouts, with varied ring radii, layer heights, angular twists, and    │
│                          │ pole positions, plus distorted cube-axis seeds and a small number of reproducible random  │
│                          │ starts. Each seed receives an annealed log-distance soft-extrema continuation with        │
│                          │ momentum, retaining the best exact squared ratio throughout. A final sharper continuation │
│                          │ polish is applied to the best candidate, emphasizing the active closest and farthest      │
│                          │ pairs while preserving the best exact configuration encountered. The search uses 10       │
│                          │ starts, 1700 continuation iterations, sharpness increasing from 5 to 260, momentum 0.84,  │
│                          │ and a final 1200-step high-sharpness polish.                                              │
