│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_ratio_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version retains the effective centered, scale-normalized smooth min/max-distance     │
│                          │ optimization, but replaces the varied early schedules with a consistently strong          │
│                          │ annealing path and adds checkpointed late-stage polishing.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The late optimizer compares the exact evaluator objective every 25 iterations. When the   │
│                          │ exact ratio declines repeatedly, it restores the best exact checkpoint, damps momentum,   │
│                          │ and reduces the step size. This prevents high-sharpness smooth gradients from drifting    │
│                          │ away from the nonsmooth active-pair optimum. Several deterministic tangent perturbation   │
│                          │ polish attempts are also used to explore nearby contact graphs while preserving           │
│                          │ reproducibility.                                                                          │
