│ patch_name               │ rollback_refinement                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add regression-aware rollback to the smooth contact refinement. The soft surrogate can    │
│                          │ deliberately decrease the exact min/diameter objective while changing contact graphs, but │
│                          │ continued deterioration often means that momentum has carried the configuration out of    │
│                          │ the strongest packing basin. The revised refinement records exact-score checkpoints more  │
│                          │ frequently. After three materially inferior checkpoints it restores the last exact-best   │
│                          │ configuration, clears momentum, damps the remaining step scale, and temporarily lowers    │
│                          │ momentum persistence. This preserves useful early basin transitions while preventing late │
│                          │ sharpness stages from spending most iterations away from the best known exact             │
│                          │ configuration.                                                                            │
