│ patch_name               │ regression_aware_rollback                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add an adaptive rollback mechanism to the refinement loop. The soft-extrema surrogate can │
│                          │ continue moving after the true nonsmooth min/max ratio has peaked, especially in the late │
│                          │ sharp phase where a small change in the active contact graph can cause a substantial      │
│                          │ evaluator regression. The existing code retains the best returned configuration, but it   │
│                          │ still spends subsequent iterations evolving inside a deteriorating basin.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The edit tracks consecutive meaningful regressions at exact-objective checkpoints. After  │
│                          │ two such regressions, it restores the last exact-best configuration, clears momentum,     │
│                          │ reduces the remaining step scale, and slightly reduces the effective sharpness. This      │
│                          │ preserves productive continuation while preventing accumulated momentum from carrying the │
│                          │ search far from its best contact structure.                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
