│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ two_tier_diverse_refinement                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the uniform full-cost restart loop with a two-tier search. The existing code      │
│                          │ spends nearly identical effort on every perturbation of one antipodal seed, even though   │
│                          │ most starts do not enter a competitive basin. The new approach performs a cheaper         │
│                          │ continuation pass on a substantially larger and more diverse population, including both   │
│                          │ gentle symmetry-breaking perturbations and several broad perturbations. It records each   │
│                          │ candidate’s best exact ratio, selects only the strongest survivors, and gives those       │
│                          │ survivors a longer high-temperature/contact-focused continuation.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reallocates approximately the same optimization budget toward basin discovery and    │
│                          │ survivor polishing. It also avoids ranking candidates solely by their final               │
│                          │ smooth-objective state: each candidate is ranked by the exact evaluator ratio encountered │
│                          │ during its first stage.                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
