│ patch_name               │ portfolio_contact_polish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 8 perturbed/geometric seeds, 3 sharpness schedules, 1450        │
│                          │ surrogate-gradient iterations per trajectory, momentum 0.82, initial step size 0.046, and │
│                          │ periodic exact-score checkpointing with restart on regressions. The revised               │
│                          │ implementation keeps the successful multi-basin continuation stage but changes its        │
│                          │ schedules, shortens it to 1250 iterations, and adds a final portfolio of exact-monotone   │
│                          │ contact-polishing branches from the globally best checkpoint.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new final branches use distinct sharpness ranges (220→650, 320→980, and 500→1450),    │
│                          │ lower local step sizes, exact evaluation of several line-search candidates at every       │
│                          │ iteration, and occasional deterministic small perturbation candidates. This separates     │
│                          │ basin discovery from high-precision active-contact optimization: surrogate dynamics can   │
│                          │ still cross contact-graph transitions early, while the final stage only retains           │
│                          │ evaluator-equivalent improvements.                                                        │
