│ patch_name               │ tiered_contact_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 18 fully independent random starts, 1450 Adam steps each, and a │
│                          │ single final 500-step polish. Its key parameters are the `6→300` beta schedules, Adam     │
│                          │ moments `(0.88, 0.96)`, learning rate `0.045→0.0045`, 18 starts, and 1450 iterations per  │
│                          │ start. This spends substantial effort refining weak random basins.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new configuration uses a two-tier allocation: 12 diverse structured and random seeds  │
│                          │ receive a cheaper 560-step broad packing stage, the best 5 candidates are selected by the │
│                          │ exact squared ratio, then only those survivors receive longer sharp continuation. It adds │
│                          │ hexagonal-layer, cube-axis, antipodal-icosahedral, and random seeds, uses normalized      │
│                          │ projected force directions rather than coordinate-wise Adam scaling, and performs several │
│                          │ deterministic symmetry-breaking survivor refinements before a high-sharpness contact      │
│                          │ polish. This concentrates computation on promising contact graphs while preserving basin  │
│                          │ diversity.                                                                                │
