│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_contact_blend                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Blend the existing smooth-extrema gradient with a bounded exact active-contact            │
│                          │ subgradient once the continuation becomes sharp. The smooth objective is valuable while   │
│                          │ contact classes are changing, but at high beta it can still assign meaningful force to    │
│                          │ pairs that are no longer true minimum or diameter constraints. The added gradient         │
│                          │ averages all pairs within 1.5% of the exact minimum and maximum squared distances, making │
│                          │ late polishing better aligned with the evaluator’s exact ratio while avoiding dependence  │
│                          │ on an arbitrary single tied contact. The blend is activated gradually as beta rises,      │
│                          │ retaining the current broad-basin behavior during early optimization.                     │
