│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the current program’s diverse structured/random restart portfolio │
│                          │ with the inspiration program’s log-distance contact gradient, checkpoint rollback, and    │
│                          │ exact-monotone multiscale polishing.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The continuation stage explores several contact graphs efficiently using normalized       │
│                          │ momentum updates. It retains exact objective checkpoints and restarts from the local best │
│                          │ state when a surrogate trajectory degrades. The final portfolio polish only accepts       │
│                          │ candidate steps that improve the evaluator-equivalent squared ratio, including multiple   │
│                          │ line-search scales and deterministic transverse perturbations. This preserves             │
│                          │ reproducibility while making the final refinement robust around nonsmooth active-contact  │
│                          │ transitions.                                                                              │
