╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ responsive_beta_retreat                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Make continuation rollback react to a single substantial exact-objective loss instead of  │
│                          │ waiting for three checkpoints. A sharp contact surrogate can cross into an inferior       │
│                          │ contact graph quickly; restoring the exact-best configuration immediately prevents        │
│                          │ subsequent momentum from reinforcing that transition. After rollback, temporarily reduce  │
│                          │ the effective sharpness so the optimizer reapproaches the contact boundary with smoother  │
│                          │ forces, then gradually resumes the scheduled beta. This directly implements a controlled  │
│                          │ beta retreat while retaining the exact score as the authoritative criterion.              │
