│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 10 initializers, 1700 broad iterations per initializer, a       │
│                          │ single 1200-step polish, soft-extrema sharpness schedules of approximately 5–260 and      │
│                          │ 55–500, fixed momentum, and exact-score checkpointing only. The new configuration retains │
│                          │ the successful staggered-hexagon family but uses fewer broad continuations and spends     │
│                          │ more effort around the best contact graph.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main addition is deterministic geometry-aware restart polishing. Perturbations are    │
│                          │ constructed from the gradient induced by near-minimum and near-maximum pair bands, with   │
│                          │ orthogonal seeded noise added at amplitudes 0.003–0.015. This targets the active shortest │
│                          │ and farthest contacts directly rather than relying only on isotropic noise. Refinement    │
│                          │ also adds rollback after repeated exact-score regressions, uses a wider late sharpness    │
│                          │ range, and finishes with a high-sharpness active-contact continuation.                    │
